@startuml
title Singleton

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Ensure one instance; provide global access.

**Motivation**:
Shared resource/config (e.g., registry) requiring single point of truth.

**Applicability**:
Exactly one instance required; globally accessible.
Resource coordination (e.g., cache, printer spooler).

**Participants & Collaborations**:
Singleton holds private static instance and accessor.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Controlled single instance; lazy init; centralized resource.
Cons: Hidden dependencies; global state hurts testability; lifecycle coupling.

**Implementation Notes**:
Thread-safe lazy init (e.g., double-checked locking) or eager init.
Prefer DI containers and scopes; replace with module-level functions in FP.

**Known Uses**:
Java Runtime, Desktop, Logger singletons in frameworks.
OS singletons (clipboard, input managers).

**Related Patterns**: Facade (single point), Monostate, Service Locator (anti-pattern vs DI).

endlegend

class Singleton {
  -instance : Singleton
  -Singleton()
  +getInstance() : Singleton
}

note right of Singleton
Private constructor
Static global accessor
Thread-safety considerations
end note
@enduml